 "transfer_protocol": {
  "_about": "How and when the worms were moved onto each assay plate -- an import directive (decision #52), not dataset metadata. The transfer time is not recorded: on a plate whose 'contrast' (lawn) video was filmed AFTER the worms went on, the transfer is taken as that video's start; otherwise as the first behaviour video's start; approximate either way. Methods: the eLife paper, Assay preparation and recording (agar plugs; eyelash pick into an S-Complete droplet for multi-density). Contrast-video order: from the gap between each plate's lawn clip and its recording, checked by eye in the videos, 2026-10-02 (Matching day 1, 2023-02-24, is worms first; days 2-3 lawn first).",
  "max_before_seconds": 300,
  "_max_before": "T is read off the first video after the transfer, so the transfer was at most this long before it (Jess Haley, 2026-10-02: 5 min; 10 would be big). On a lawn-first plate the lawn clip's end bounds it more tightly when closer.",
  "hand_written_tolerance_seconds": [60, 60],
  "_hand_written": "Pick (growthTimePicked) and food-deprivation (starvedTime) times were read off a clock -- possibly analog (e.g. an Apple Watch face) -- and written to the minute: +/- 60 s covers a truncated digital reading and a by-eye analog one (Jess Haley, 2026-10-02).",
  "rules": [
   {
    "source_folder": "foragingConcentration",
    "method": "agar plug, through an empty NGM plate",
    "contrast_video": "before_worms"
   },
   {
    "source_folder": "foragingMini",
